    problem: "1,925,946 of 2,150,540 Panda training videos have only one caption; multi-view tokenizer (num_latent_tokens=4) is starved of per-view positives. The three legacy additions (147K BLIP-style + 77K VideoLLaMA-style + earlier addition_1.json) cover only 10.4% with mixed styles, hurting k-means token routing. The current 2.15M anchor (P14 c=4096 l=3 CanHit@100=95.57) was trained with num_latent_tokens=1 because pseudo queries were not ready. Without unified high-coverage diverse pseudo queries, the multi-view core contribution cannot be evaluated at scale.",
    objective: "Build a pseudo-query generation pipeline that (a) generates aspect-aware diverse captions for all 2.15M Panda training videos under a single unified style, (b) tunes captions-per-video as a hyperparameter with quality-aware adaptive stopping (floor=4), (c) compares the existing local VideoLLaMA pipeline against one community-validated <=8B VLM challenger, and (d) retrains GRDR with num_latent_tokens=4 + pseudo queries on the 100K pilot then 2.15M full set to beat the current NLT=1 Panda anchor at matched compact budget.",
    motivation: "Multi-view video tokenizer is the No. 1 contribution per CLAUDE.md, but the recent 2.15M Panda anchor was trained with num_latent_tokens=1 because pseudo queries were not ready. CLAUDE.md says the multi-view decomposition must be preserved unless there is a strong reviewer-proof reason. This package closes the prerequisite-data gap so the core contribution claim can be re-established at scale, and provides a generation pipeline reusable for downstream paper experiments.",
    hypothesis: "A unified-style pseudo-query dataset with 4-10 captions per video (visual-richness adaptive, floor 4), 6-aspect diversity (main action / people / object-scene / screen text / there-is / talking-head), generated by the winner of a VideoLLaMA-vs-Qwen3-VL-8B bake-off, enables a GRDR num_latent_tokens=4 + pseudo-queries checkpoint on 2.15M Panda to match or beat the current num_latent_tokens=1 anchor (Panda Setting 1 CanHit@100 = 95.57) at matched compact budget (avg_candidates_per_query <= 310), with non-negative zero-shot transfer to the four downstream datasets (MSR-VTT / ActivityNet / DiDeMo / LSMDC) Setting 1.",
    noChangeBoundary: "Source video corpus (2.15M Panda train videos), InternVideo2 features, X-Pool reranker checkpoints, the existing 818K c=512 Panda baseline anchor, Stage-1 to Stage-2 handoff, progressive co-training schedule (3-loop), and BARS-on inference policy are all out of scope. The multi-view tokenizer architecture and contrastive-loss routing logic are not modified; only the supervision data and num_latent_tokens setting change.",
